OpenCode is an open-source, model-agnostic AI coding agent that runs in
the terminal.  It combines a full-screen TUI and a scriptable CLI with a
client/server architecture, LSP awareness, and multi-session support, and
can talk to dozens of model providers (or local models).

This port builds OpenCode and its OpenTUI terminal engine from source
using Bun, and ships the result as a single self-contained executable
with the Bun runtime and the web UI assets embedded.

The interactive TUI requires OpenTUI's native Zig core, which upstream
does not ship for FreeBSD, so the port builds it from source as well.
